fter us :)","Images":["https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/grass-cs/ACvplmOXQmIMbXdm94mkIAKxG8Yla1L15msuK_hEF4kjoarBJGTTXJtX68UcJ1XQy9wKrkt7O7cBXni_CpItDqMwqZ4LgiU-a1LCjZ3LwWdSOwlUA1ebY1hCRREyHt_PsuPMhVacKw6uQix9U4P4=k-no","https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/grass-cs/ACvplmPdPNi6hLqv8sBvvbsGTsnqEWzNWfqVqG08n45sY8U8TSuKGjLFYobB51ClIUEJbqKyzRAU2gcyjRkR6WLy_q2x9Gd3jKqKuZ7CJk1AHqPSQWvyKkg7FzW9XOqnkVLAdFS-EqhzZR8GuDZN=k-no","https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/grass-cs/ACvplmN83749-ykbmyH_xO3JbS3Z5e2ubykB-FjnfUhO8SfOkqsG6fy7yKJ6hBNyjdC50oWRqRnITuTHNrl4J3wnHNCgSyOOdfpkAo7MHAMsLxDqv9ue_siKBcELUEaysWX8kUxIHlAsMbXMeIE=k-no","https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/grass-cs/ACvplmO6jQMPKFAU3l0kUl66LP8IVhDBqYLZUUw9dHiExOc2DShgsHKds120aWyePJBLuyYxjxQDDUTFNrhbQcGBHgM4R6SNXD8qkY1tTCrxg2FHxVmDBZ4U0XarXeWuFp8icWs0KQyfSwB-rafm=k-no"],"When":"4 months ago","review_id":"Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tadWQwbGxWM2wwVkRobVVtWXpOa1ptTmxBemFXYxAB","source":"Google","rating_scale":5,"rating_float":5,"author_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115955380234056454950/reviews?hl=en-GB","posted_at_unix_micros":1780236214160377,"updated_at_unix_micros":1780236214160377,"language":"en","translated_lang":"","text_original":"I went here with my family for brunch and all the food was 10/10, especially the French toast. The drinks were amazing too - we ordered lattes, Raspberry Matcha and Chaii latte. Cannot fault the customer service, it was just a lovely atmosphere a big shout out to Kenza for looking after us :)","text_translated":"","published_at":"2026-05-31T14:03:34.160377Z"},{"Name":"Adrian","ProfilePicture":"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKwAiBqZtPT61N7ouuPfDs6pQfgjQdXF5152mGhBvEo_XnYzQ=s120-c-rp-mo-ba12-br100","Rating":5,"Description":"Impeccable brunch spot. I had their black \u0026 blue french toast (special menu) which I thoroughly enjoyed. The blackberry and jalapeno jam was so unique and unlike anything I've ever had, yet paired so well with the rest of the dish. It was also incredibly filling. The only thing that let me down was the matcha, which just tasted like milk. Still, extremely solid brunch options here.","Images":["https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/grass-cs/ACvplmOokx4rDvTHG6roFDTK71kZn0UjsQtf7ymaiNBfanDOM0kKTfGTJr9f3dA4b6U86cZX6B0J5tEvcaPxPxy33gFgyJ87pNEGtMQcen-_-fmd7G8nCDrCLyD08QtnHWxqDmuSdxTevjIU2J4=k-no","https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/grass-cs/ACvplmN3KiFcfU_oBLPV7G6tRXORz1pR-8x7Vy664oT1K-JfTXdtavFaxYypBxlQUYZgEptb97lgnsI-w0WCJjrWeQ_GPGtb8K3trlmqn7msIJzFa8Wn7sXnqFGmpJIisYuXzhoxYpaSqAjmtRaL=k-no","https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/grass-cs/ACvplmNbEl5IGnBS4pyECRB_zw81uIxIpat5RTZwY7X30VK70Vid2o2MoDY3BS4JKMbtwLp3TtHYdmXGvsgCZ6a_L6-WgRA-VVTod-d7LgmEuLwDsN28wMtIwKICoBw72oAojXKdR-DTrUzAebFC=k-no","https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/grass-cs/ACvplmP2nZeQKTjGCML5vwB5k8h_wIu6H0XJkZMIoycKV2EOd8WrYDWTz9FQH9TTSMD9iaWorTVNKf0P9RMtSpSqnHOC46-deLu3XEYMsN8XJHYJYx1Mus6a48XxxfJq4Q0G-cJr1qUBDsG8sHA=k-no"],"When":"a month ago","review_id":"Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2toeVZqTnFUR2hWYUZkSGEyZE9ZblJ2YjFCMVpFRRAB","source":"Google","rating_scale":5,"rating_float":5,"author_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/102032798880687442044/reviews?hl=en-GB","posted_at_unix_micros":1786028049637026,"updated_at_unix_micros":1786028049637026,"language":"en","translated_lang":"","text_original":"Impeccable brunch spot. I had their black \u0026 blue french toast (special menu) which I thoroughly enjoyed. The blackberry and jalapeno jam was so unique and unlike anything I've ever had, yet paired so well with the rest of the dish. It was also incredibly filling. The only thing that let me down was the matcha, which just tasted like milk. Still, extremely solid brunch options here.","text_translated":"","published_at":"2026-08-06T14:54:09.637026Z"},{"Name":"saqar shojaei","ProfilePicture":"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVjqWZcYtJ1VTT1zea5mG5DKQbLuuMBF7sGUK29CxsxsdK9V5Q4=s120-c-rp-mo-ba12-br100","Rating":5,"Description":"The atmosphere here is great, and the staff are really friendly. Our order was ready quite quickly. There’s usually plenty of seating during the week, but I’d recommend booking for the weekend to avoid any wait. Every dish we’ve tried has been delicious. They also have a special offer with a different menu, we went on Sunday and absolutely loved it.","Images":["https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/grass-cs/ACvplmPbuGvAKTkDIfPSqKwpEMhR0VPjwfOyhHk_0-5JffwEdeJPHkPiHiyaPGtFWcTtdxaOn9oY-0-Py1Ou8e8XltyDqLos_Ab1ul0RBvYGo4J374Kl25TpxZSUIeCNh2ONwoccWLVx5cl9unym=k-no","https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/grass-cs/ACvplmP0U3XTPr6-Y7QlzT9jEFfvNyTYvxKWjcEWJjZlBmH8-g6gYQ1h-3zpigX4tTFb1B1SZBDCxHhYT60sOAtn8ySvMY_YU6hIfHgG_HD5NJdjEwGq7f8mizgXJQpfNFPN3Vpg4N2s74TnCJmy=k-no","https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/grass-cs/ACvplmMS2kd5T9gqkcr3hMS5FteGVM6F2b3rnghh2bPpQyo6El22LSivQcK4rVXJGCFT9d8L2jN_qVsUj0lHt1Qs6Oyuddiyym-_5Dfzo-BoV-006muyDwIBqzBrUmRxspnk1D6Xuqa4RtxPsgr7=k-no"],"When":"5 months ago","review_id":"Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21sclMzaFpkMlU1Um5ObVpHcDVPV2RHVXpoWlIxRRAB","source":"Google","rating_scale":5,"rating_float":5,"author_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105255621036367570236/reviews?hl=en-GB","posted_at_unix_micros":1776527052836678,"updated_at_unix_micros":1776527052836678,"language":"en","translated_lang":"","text_original":"The atmosphere here is great, and the staff are really friendly. Our order was ready quite quickly. There’s usually plenty of seating during the week, but I’d recommend booking for the weekend to avoid any wait. Every dish we’ve tried has been delicious. They also have a special offer with a different menu, we went on Sunday and absolutely loved it.","text_translated":"","published_at":"2026-04-18T15:44:12.836678Z"},{"Name":"Eric Chan","ProfilePicture":"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVeLJiG6uqkpGs5iafQW7gzvC2_3R0PVEyR6ypyyvcos6A8-bQk_g=s120-c-rp-mo-ba12-br100","Rating":4,"Description":"Pot Kettle Black is one of those places I’m generally happy to return to. The space is open, warm, and inviting, and it feels like a nice spot to slow down a bit, especially for brunch or a catch-up.\n\nIt does get pretty crowded on weekends, so expect a bit of noise and waiting around. Front-of-house service was prompt and friendly when we arrived, which helped, though the kitchen was noticeably slower. Food took a while to come out, but nothing outrageous, just something to be aware of if you’re in a rush.\n\nFood itself was pretty decent across the board. Nothing overcomplicated, just well-executed brunch dishes that do what they’re meant to. The real standout for me was the coffee. Easily one of the better cups in Manchester. Balanced, well made, and clearly something they take seriously here. That alone makes the place worth coming back to.\n\nPrices felt fair for the location and quality, especially given how central Barton Arcade is. You don’t feel like you’re being overcharged just for sitting somewhere trendy, which I appreciate.\n\nOverall, it’s a nice, dependable place to meet friends, chat, and enjoy a good coffee. Go when you’re not in a rush, expect it to be busy on weekends, and you’ll likely leave feeling satisfied rather than stressed.","Images":["https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/grass-cs/ACvplmMjiMbEVMcWlwcIMEy4RXTlzYOrOmFQ3gImKU4xx_R4QJcpyy5POrssF8bTIAdM5Bv7dKQyc9QA5XtSJuwtKzCkevpq7_h2narMFP_nLU5pDfrRdOwpmxFSQcAzrSwcKC-N3rk8RgXkA9UV=k-no","https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/grass-cs/ACvplmNZBKXKlBNSa9px0MoBI6td0VRc6kQArpxw3CGXUtGtzoqveVKIAd0sBsZLuRsIZmK03dR3sJca5bDZ6N8LubgaxqIQDaCgV1SbQhMHzHEtKBoU0WwOmeJNIMQEjY7wAs-HSmlvKHLA-4c=k-no","https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/grass-cs/ACvplmPZ3BZ2biAFUauQenU0_hbU71E5shTDsaGexEOUrSwmuVe_jpj6Cd1ZGhl2SwJv9HpLMZhZq146G9hdTGOqZAV248UZYXPns_rxXTxops7-ZC-ZqsQi4WwAJXu0TEXuQtTvI7jYUVOLPW0n=k-no","https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/grass-cs/ACvplmONufc8X44qEAqD8Nx85Lb-nLiPxQJiTXK1wpFpceuFSMAiUkwRkyH1vYcCRx3LeN-QcVLnizlP8AnZUTQpVKeSPJvyefvCL5FMJ194SY3EvqjxTi9PzUChwXqIOClE0aIikryM-KzX14-F=k-no","https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/grass-cs/ACvplmP_jkv7x-z5XcAy6nCSXpIXr8LYothXR7O-ZGs0pF4YlNyOcdxBt_nlrk34GyIJIAm97Syy0IsflEelonm33Zr9HsTUWDCJF-aVJjWSQ-5eDFd6DNkfTYUQVz0PvVzXCFqjJifjKracM1-v=k-no"],"When":"Edited 8 months ago","review_id":"Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xWclRHbzBRVE4wWkV3M1ExbEljVlJuZDNKMlRsRRAB","source":"Google","rating_scale":5,"rating_float":4,"author_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105475796314773451297/reviews?hl=en-GB","posted_at_unix_micros":1765679060228496,"updated_at_unix_micros":1768764345054258,"language":"en","translated_lang":"","text_original":"Pot Kettle Black is one of those places I’m generally happy to return to. The space is open, warm, and inviting, and it feels like a nice spot to slow down a bit, especially for brunch or a catch-up.\n\nIt does get pretty crowded on weekends, so expect a bit of noise and waiting around. Front-of-house service was prompt and friendly when we arrived, which helped, though the kitchen was noticeably slower. Food took a while to come out, but nothing outrageous, just something to be aware of if you’re in a rush.\n\nFood itself was pretty decent across the board. Nothing overcomplicated, just well-executed brunch dishes that do what they’re meant to. The real standout for me was the coffee. Easily one of the better cups in Manchester. Balanced, well made, and clearly something they take seriously here. That alone makes the place worth coming back to.\n\nPrices felt fair for the location and quality, especially given how central Barton Arcade is. You don’t feel like you’re being overcharged just for sitting somewhere trendy, which I appreciate.\n\nOverall, it’s a nice, dependable place to meet friends, chat, and enjoy a good coffee. Go when you’re not in a rush, expect it to be busy on weekends, and you’ll likely leave feeling satisfied rather than stressed.","text_translated":"","published_at":"2025-12-14T02:24:20.228496Z"},{"Name":"Raul","ProfilePicture":"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-